[
    "The insured has paid the premium mentioned in the Schedule as consideration for insurance in respect of accidental loss or damage occurring during the Period of Insurance.",
    "The term "two wheeler" in this policy includes motorcycle, scooter, autocycle or any other motorised two-wheeled vehicle mentioned in the Schedule.",
    "Section I of the policy indemnifies the insured against loss of or damage to the vehicle insured and/or its accessories whilst thereon, subject to the policy's terms, exceptions and conditions.",
    "Section I (in its first listing) identifies the following perils as causes of loss or damage covered: fire, explosion, self-ignition or lightning; burglary, housebreaking or theft; riot and strike; earthquake (fire and shock damage); flood, typhoon, hurricane, storm, tempest, inundation, cyclone, hailstorm, frost; and accidental external means.",
    "The insurer will indemnify insured loss arising from accidental loss or damage to the vehicle's CNG/LPG kit subject to the Insured’s Declared Value of the kit specified in the Schedule.",
    "IMT26 (Fire and/or Theft Risks Only) states that Section II of the policy is cancelled for that endorsement.",
    "Under IMT26, the insurer's liability under Section I is limited to loss or damage by specified perils (including fire, explosion, self-ignition, lightning, burglary, housebreaking, theft, riot, strike, malicious damage, terrorism, storm, tempest, flood, inundation and earthquake) while the vehicle is laid up in a garage and not in use.",
    "The IMT26 clause includes a note that in the case of Fire Risk only, the words "burglary housebreaking theft" are to be deleted.",
    "IMT33 (Loss of Accessories), applicable to motorised two wheeler policies only, provides that upon payment of an additional premium and subject to declaration, the insurer will indemnify the insured for loss of or damage to accessories that are the property of the insured caused by burglary, housebreaking or theft, subject to the policy's other terms and conditions.",
    "IMT33 requires the insured to have specifically declared the accessories to obtain indemnity for their loss or damage under that clause.",
    "The Auto Secure Two Wheeler Package Policy includes add-on covers, one of which is TA16 Depreciation Allowance.",
    "TA16 Depreciation Allowance is applicable only if it is shown on the policy schedule.",
    "A later version of Section I.A expands covered perils to include malicious act, terrorist activity, transit by road, rail, inland-waterway, lift, elevator or air, and landslide/rockslide in addition to previously listed perils.",
    "Section I(B) titled "LOSS OF OR DAMAGE TO THE VEHICLE INSURED (OD without Theft)" indemnifies the insured against loss or damage to the vehicle and/or its accessories whilst thereon except for loss or damage due to burglary, housebreaking or theft.",
    "Section I(B) lists covered perils for OD without Theft as fire, explosion, self-ignition or lightning; riot and strike; earthquake (fire and shock damage); flood, typhoon, hurricane, storm, tempest, inundation, cyclone, hailstorm, frost; accidental external means; malicious act; terrorist activity; transit by road, rail, inland-waterway, lift, elevator or air; and landslide/rockslide.",
    "Where parts are replaced, the policy provides for a deduction for depreciation at specified rates.",
    "The specified depreciation rates include: 50% for all rubber/nylon/plastic parts, tyres and tubes, batteries and air bags; and 30% for fibre glass components.",
    "Multiple clauses in the document state that indemnities and endorsements are subject to the terms, exceptions, conditions, limitations and exceptions of the policy."
] 

